{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 824, "block_type": "heading", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2."], "text": "Goal MOB-2.", "extra": {"heading_level": 3, "style": "Heading 3"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 825, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2."], "text": "The City will maintain and enhance a safe, convenient, balanced, efficient and interconnected multi-modal system consisting of vehicular, transit, bicycle, and pedestrian transportation options; and will be coordinated with the City’s Comprehensive Plan while maintaining the economic viability of the City’s businesses, and continued enhancement of the quality of life for the City’s neighborhoods.

"], "text": "Goal MOB-2.", "extra": {"heading_level": 3, "style": "Heading 3"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 825, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2."], "text": "The City will maintain and enhance a safe, convenient, balanced, efficient and interconnected multi-modal system consisting of vehicular, transit, bicycle, and pedestrian transportation options; and will be coordinated with the City’s Comprehensive Plan while maintaining the economic viability of the City’s businesses, and continued enhancement of the quality of life for the City’s neighborhoods.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 826, "block_type": "heading", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1."], "text": "Objective MOB-2.1.", "extra": {"heading_level": 4, "style": "Heading 4"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 827, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1."], "text": "All roads within the City are classified as roads within Existing Urbanized Areas by the State of Florida, and are within the Urban Infill Area (UIA) by Miami-Dade County. The City shall strive to operate all roadways at a level of service better than the LOS Standards contained in the adopted policies of this element. The LOS standards for traffic facilities shall be used in the Concurrency Management Program (CMP) to issue development orders as of the effective date provided in CMP as set forth in the Capital Improvements Element.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 828, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1."], "text": "(Ord. No. 2025-14, 06/10/25)", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 829, "block_type": "heading", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2.1.1."], "text": "Policy MOB-2.1.1.", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 830, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2.1.1."], "text": "The minimum or lowest quality acceptable peakperiod* operating LOS standards for State Principal Arterial, Minor Arterial, County Minor Arterial, County and City Collector roads within the City shall be the minimum acceptable peakperiod LOS standard:", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 831, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.

", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2.1.1."], "text": "The minimum or lowest quality acceptable peakperiod* operating LOS standards for State Principal Arterial, Minor Arterial, County Minor Arterial, County and City Collector roads within the City shall be the minimum acceptable peakperiod LOS standard:", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 831, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2.1.1."], "text": "Where public transit service does not exist, roadways shall operate at or above LOS E; within the Special Transportation Area (STA) twenty (20%) percent of nonState roads may operate below LOS E. All County roads within the STA will maintain LOS standards consistent with the County adopted standards.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 832, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2.1.1."], "text": "Where public transit service having headways of twenty (20) minutes or less is provided within 1/2 mile distance, roadways shall operate at no greater than one-hundred twenty (120%) percent of their capacity;", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 833, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2.1.1."], "text": "Where commuter rail or express bus public transit service exists, generally parallel roads within ½ mile shall operate at no greater than one-hundred fifty (150%) percent of their capacity.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 834, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2.1.1."], "text": "* Peak period means the average of the two highest consecutive hours of traffic volume during a weekday.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 835, "block_type": "heading", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2-1.2."], "text": "Policy MOB-2-1.2.", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 836, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2-1.2."], "text": "Roadways that are physically or environmentally constrained or legislatively prohibited from expansion due to their valued historic, or cultural character, will be allowed to operate at a LOS above the minimum established LOS standards. These roadways will continue to operate at such a level that significant degradation does not occur based on conditions existing at the time of local government comprehensive plan adoption.

", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "block_index": 836, "block_type": "paragraph", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.1.", "Policy MOB-2-1.2."], "text": "Roadways that are physically or environmentally constrained or legislatively prohibited from expansion due to their valued historic, or cultural character, will be allowed to operate at a LOS above the minimum established LOS standards. These roadways will continue to operate at such a level that significant degradation does not occur based on conditions existing at the time of local government comprehensive plan adoption. For roadways in urbanized areas such as the City, significant degradation means (1) an increase in average annual daily traffic of 10 percent above the maximum service volume, or (2) a reduction in operating speed for the peak direction in the 100th highest hour of 10 percent below the speed of the adopted LOS standard. The following roads are designated Constrained Facilities:", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
