{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b129__c0__1ea72cfd6946", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Future Land Use Element", "Goal FLU-1.", "Objective FLU-1.6."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 129, "text": "Objective FLU-1.6.", "extra": {"heading_level": 4, "style": "Heading 4"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b130__c0__716d866c9a55", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Future Land Use Element", "Goal FLU-1.", "Objective FLU-1.6."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 130, "text": "Coordinate the City’s actions with appropriate resource planning and management plans prepared pursuant to Chapter 380, F.S., as amended.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b131__c0__2072c5485a32", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Future Land Use Element", "Goal FLU-1.", "Objective FLU-1.6.", "Policy FLU-1.6.1."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 131, "text": "Policy FLU-1.6.1.", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b132__c0__ef03ff886e3b", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Future Land Use Element", "Goal FLU-1.", "Objective FLU-1.6.", "Policy FLU-1.6.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 132, "text": "Coordinate with State, regional, county and local agencies to ensure mutual cooperation in the development of all appropriate resource planning and management plans prepared pursuant to Chapter 380, F.S. as amended. The City will continue to monitor all other local governments’ activities when notice is provided. The City will continue to provide notice as required to other local governments and agencies on upcoming large development projects. The City will continue to work closely with the South Florida Regional Planning Council, Miami-Dade County School Board and the State Department of Community Affairs on regional issues. The City will continue to maintain mutual aid agreements with other local governments with reference to fire service, police and disaster preparedness.

