{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b465__c0__a6b8206b710d", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-2.", "Objective COM-2.1.", "Policy COM-2.1.11."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 465, "text": "Policy COM-2.1.11.", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b466__c0__5ee9e764c638", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-2.", "Objective COM-2.1.", "Policy COM-2.1.11."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 466, "text": "The City shall ensure that sanitary sewer facilities are provided to meet projected future demands as they are realized, at the required LOS. Facilities to meet new demands shall be provided for by those creating that demand and funded through the sanitary sewer impact fee. Such provision of facilities shall be by construction, payment of impact fees, or taxes, which shall lead to construction, or by binding agreement for construction assuring that required facilities are available to meet the concurrency requirements of this plan. Future demand estimates should be used to aid in the sizing and scheduling of such facilities, however, construction of facilities need only occur where actual demand is realized, and when such facilities will provide for operation at no less than the LOS standard applicable. The City shall coordinate with MiamiDade Water and Sewer Authority to monitor and exchange information and management practices to insure LOS standards are being maintained.

