{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b505__c0__510940ce6c90", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.3."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 505, "text": "Issue development orders only to projects that meet or exceed the minimum acceptable LOS standards for drainage and flood protection as reviewed through the City’s Concurrency Management Program.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b506__c0__f569c85c5885", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.4."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 506, "text": "Policy COM-4.1.4.", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b507__c0__9b3dc184dc10", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.4."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 507, "text": "Assist property owners with general information related to flood zone per Federal Emergency Management Agency (FEMA) maps and available floodproofing technology. Flood prone areas which represent substantial risk for occupants during disaster events should be considered for corrective action or targeted for special attention during disaster response actions.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b508__c0__d93d9d24742b", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.5."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 508, "text": "Policy COM-4.1.5.", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b509__c0__b3280e27fb92", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.5."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 509, "text": "The minimum acceptable Flood Protection LOS standards for the City shall be protection from the degree of flooding that would result for a duration of one day from a ten-year storm. All structures shall be constructed at, or above, the minimum floor elevation specified in the Flood Insurance Rate Maps for Coral Gables in Miami-Dade County, Florida. All new development must retain at least the first one inch (1\") of storm water runoff onsite, or other nonpublic sites as may be secured for permanent services. Designs to meet this first inch criteria will be reviewed for design solutions to meet actual site conditions.

", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.5."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 509, "text": "The minimum acceptable Flood Protection LOS standards for the City shall be protection from the degree of flooding that would result for a duration of one day from a ten-year storm. All structures shall be constructed at, or above, the minimum floor elevation specified in the Flood Insurance Rate Maps for Coral Gables in Miami-Dade County, Florida. All new development must retain at least the first one inch (1\") of storm water runoff onsite, or other nonpublic sites as may be secured for permanent services. Designs to meet this first inch criteria will be reviewed for design solutions to meet actual site conditions. The burden for the construction of such facilities shall be borne by the developer and/or owner of such sites. Failure of such facilities and subsequent corrections shall also be the responsibility of the developer and/or owner. The City may require greater than the first one inch onsite retention where the City establishes more restrictive rules in the public interest.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b510__c0__0c0dfcfe9415", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.6."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 510, "text": "Policy COM-4.1.6.", "extra": {"heading_level": 5, "style": "Heading 5"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b511__c0__118e3f747dbc", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.6."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 511, "text": "Promote the use of water conservation measures in stormwater management through the use of onsite retention of storm water, use of native vegetation with low water requirements to reduce irrigation demands, and community education in water conservation practices in development site planning and drainage design. This policy was revised beyond the EAR recommendations due to further review.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b512__c0__620b92acaaf4", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-4.", "Objective COM-4.1.", "Policy COM-4.1.6."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 512, "text": "Potable Water.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b513__c0__18e8798446e7", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-5."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 513, "text": "Goal COM-5.", "extra": {"heading_level": 3, "style": "Heading 3"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b514__c0__9cab5c927da3", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Community Facilities Element", "Goal COM-5."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 514, "text": "The City of Coral Gables shall ensure that a safe potable water supply with sufficient quantity and quality to serve the City is available.

