{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b860__c0__f8c3888c24d2", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.2.", "Policy MOB-2.2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 860, "text": "A proposed development will not be denied a concurrency approval for transportation facilities provided that the development is otherwise consistent with the adopted Comprehensive Plan and it meets the following criteria pursuant to Section 163.3180 (5) (b), Florida Statutes, as amended:", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b861__c0__0f36805039fe", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.2.", "Policy MOB-2.2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 861, "text": "The proposed development is located within the Gables Redevelopment and Infill District.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b862__c0__6ae5e5368f18", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.2.", "Policy MOB-2.2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 862, "text": "If the project would result in an increase in peak-period traffic volume on a Florida Intrastate Highway System (FIHA).", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b863__c0__0a327f890e42", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Mobility Element", "Goal MOB-2.", "Objective MOB-2.2.", "Policy MOB-2.2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 863, "text": "FIHA roadway that is operating below any adopted LOS standard, which increase would exceed two (2%) percent of the capacity of the roadway at the adopted LOS standard, the City shall require the developer and successors to implement and maintain trip reduction measures to reduce travel by single-occupant vehicles so that the resultant increase in traffic volume does not exceed two (2%) percent.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
