{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1400__c0__dcf93b492d28", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1400, "text": "Automatic fire suppression systems shall be required in all buildings of six floors or more.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1401__c0__7299c7c6dc94", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1401, "text": "Adequate Water Distribution LOS Standards. The City shall seek to provide adequate water distribution and hydrants for all existing and new areas annexed and serviced by the Fire Department. All existing and new water distribution systems, fire hydrants and flows shall be in compliance with the National Fire Protection Standards (NFPA) and Insurance Services Office (ISO) requirements, as amended.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1402__c0__a746e9f21863", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1.

These sites serve to preserve the aesthetic quality of an area or to intersperse congested urban environments with aesthetically pleasing buffer areas. Some open space areas may serve as linear parks or vest pocket parks, while other areas are parkways, boulevard medians, plazas, malls, courthouse squares and promenades.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1405__c0__404d5835427c", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1405, "text": "Neighborhood Parks those designated areas that are “walk-to” facilities where residents may walk or bicycle to the park within a given neighborhood. Areas for diverse recreational activities which may include, but are not limited to the following: field games; court games; sports fields; playground apparatus area; picnic area; landscaping and gardens areas; and senior citizen areas. The Neighborhood Park is a place where neighbors and their families go to meet.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1406__c0__8e60f4df036f", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1406, "text": "Community Facilities is an area that provides a diverse range of recreational and leisure activities or provides very specific active recreation facilities for all individuals and families. Facilities and activities may include, but are not limited to athletic fields, swimming pools, gymnasiums, performing and community centers. These facilities are designed to meet the recreation needs of the entire community.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1407__c0__afef01a7b000", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1407, "text": "Non-City District/Regional Parks is an area selected for its natural and ornamental quality and its suitability of which the purpose is to function as a regionally-based recreational activity area. Recreational activities could include, but not be limited to, swimming, picnicking, camping, boating, fishing, and a variety of trail uses.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1408__c0__a3305793b32b", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1408, "text": "Public School Facilities LOS: Coordinate new residential development with the future availability of public school facilities consistent with the adopted level of service (LOS) standards for public school concurrency to ensure the inclusion of those projects necessary to address existing deficiencies in the 5-year schedule of capital improvements, and meet future needs based upon achieving and maintaining the adopted level of service standards throughout the planning period. Beginning January 1, 2008, the adopted LOS standard for all Miami-Dade County Public Schools facilities is 100% utilization of Florida Inventory of School Houses (FISH) Capacity (with relocatable classrooms).

", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1408, "text": "Public School Facilities LOS: Coordinate new residential development with the future availability of public school facilities consistent with the adopted level of service (LOS) standards for public school concurrency to ensure the inclusion of those projects necessary to address existing deficiencies in the 5-year schedule of capital improvements, and meet future needs based upon achieving and maintaining the adopted level of service standards throughout the planning period. Beginning January 1, 2008, the adopted LOS standard for all Miami-Dade County Public Schools facilities is 100% utilization of Florida Inventory of School Houses (FISH) Capacity (with relocatable classrooms). This LOS standard, except for magnet schools, shall be applicable in each public school concurrency service area (CSA), defined as the public school attendance boundary established by Miami-Dade County Public Schools.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1409__c0__797e1365ab03", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1409, "text": "The adopted LOS standard for Magnet Schools is 100% of FISH (With Relocatable Classrooms), which shall be calculated on a districtwide basis.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1410__c0__f1327c5070f6", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1410, "text": "LOS standards for public school facilities apply to those traditional educational facilities, owned and operated by Miami-Dade County Public Schools, that are required to serve the residential development within their established Concurrency Service Area. LOS standards do not apply to charter schools, however, the capacity of both charter and magnet schools is credited against the impact of development. No credit against the impact of development shall be given for either magnet or charter schools if their enrollment is at, or above, 100% FISH capacity.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1411__c0__97b176c3e136", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-1.", "Objective CIE-1.2.", "Policy CIE-1.2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1411, "text": "Certification of the availability and commitment of capacity by Miami-Dade County Public Schools during the concurrency review process shall be sufficient to demonstrate that such facilities are available to meet the impacts of a residential development.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
