"], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1474, "text": "The City maintains a 5-Year Capital Improvement Program (CIP) containing projects that are financially feasible and necessary due to deficiencies in levels of service identified in other Comprehensive Plan elements or are other capital improvements which the City has determined shall be included in its CIP in provision of public services at or above the minimum LOS standards as adopted.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1475__c0__3150c1dc7d11", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-2.", "Objective CIE-2.1."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 1475, "text": "Objective CIE-2.1.", "extra": {"heading_level": 4, "style": "Heading 4"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1476__c0__b039be5de013", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-2.", "Objective CIE-2.1."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1476, "text": "The City, as part of its annual fiscal year budget approval process, via that process, shall incorporate the new CIP into the Comprehensive Plan. The CIP shall be an Appendix to this document", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1477__c0__d699a0592cd8", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-2.", "Objective CIE-2.2."], "block_type": "heading", "block_index": 1477, "text": "Objective CIE-2.2.", "extra": {"heading_level": 4, "style": "Heading 4"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1478__c0__57bdc627b4bf", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-2.", "Objective CIE-2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1478, "text": "Pursuant to Chapter 163, Florida Statutes, the Miami-Dade County Educational Facilities Plan and the Five-Year Facilities Work Program for 2024-2025 through 2029-2030 developed by Miami-Dade County Public Schools and adopted by the Miami-Dade County School Board, is incorporated by reference into the City’s Capital Improvement Plan, as applicable.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1479__c0__3aab17d8ac14", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-2.", "Objective CIE-2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1479, "text": "The City of Coral Gables shall coordinate with Miami-Dade County Public Schools to annually update its Facilities Work Program to include existing and anticipated facilities for both the 5-year and long-term planning periods, and to ensure that the adopted LOS standard, including interim standards, will continue to be achieved and maintained. The City of Coral Gables, through its annual updates of the 5-year Capital Improvements Element and Program, will incorporate by reference the latest adopted Miami-Dade County Public Schools Facilities Work Program for educational facilities.

", "Objective CIE-2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1479, "text": "The City of Coral Gables shall coordinate with Miami-Dade County Public Schools to annually update its Facilities Work Program to include existing and anticipated facilities for both the 5-year and long-term planning periods, and to ensure that the adopted LOS standard, including interim standards, will continue to be achieved and maintained. The City of Coral Gables, through its annual updates of the 5-year Capital Improvements Element and Program, will incorporate by reference the latest adopted Miami-Dade County Public Schools Facilities Work Program for educational facilities. The City of Coral Gables and Miami-Dade County Public Schools will coordinate their planning efforts prior to and during the City’s Comprehensive Land Use Plan amendment process, and during updates to the Miami-Dade County Public Schools Facilities Work Program.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1480__c0__56b0f985d398", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Capital Improvements Element", "Goal CIE-2.", "Objective CIE-2.2."], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1480, "text": "The Miami-Dade County Public Schools Facilities Work Program will be evaluated on an annual basis to ensure that the LOS standards will continue to be achieved and maintained throughout the planning period.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
