{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1585__c0__e33c36caf6d6", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Green Initiatives Element", "Goal GRN-1.", "Transportation"], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1585, "text": "Policy GRN-1.3.8.", "extra": {"style": "Body Text"}}
{"id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan__b1586__c0__5650912c788e", "doc_id": "Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan", "source_path": "/workspaces/civicai-mvp/data/raw/Coral_Gables_Comprehensive_Plan.docx", "section_path": ["Administration Element", "Green Initiatives Element", "Goal GRN-1.", "Transportation"], "block_type": "paragraph", "block_index": 1586, "text": "The City will strive to reduce greenhouse gas emissions by continuing to implement efficient, compact, pedestrian-friendly land use planning and zoning initiatives with the goal of lowering automobile vehicle miles traveled and vehicle hours traveled while increasing energy efficiency. Vehicle hours traveled is recognized as a means of reducing driver delay while also reducing excess fuel consumption in congested traffic.

